# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is the reproducible RESEARCH ARTIFACT (code + data) AND the
# manuscript source (paper/), version-controlled together (as in Paper 1).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# LaTeX build cruft only (the paper/ source, PDF, DOCX, and figures ARE committed)
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/_c*.png

# Reproduction data IS committed, so a git clone / Code Ocean capsule reproduces
# the article's numbers with no external download (same model as Paper 1). Tracked:
#   data/raw/*.csv                  frozen captures, the object of record (incl. raw_response)
#   data/outcomes/ground_truth.json Altman Z'' labels the analysis grades against
#   docs/*.json                     reported financials those labels derive from
#   data/frozen/*.freeze.json       per-capture SHA-256 receipts (also in DATA_MANIFEST.md)

# Legacy price context for the INACTIVE directional task (not used by the credit
# reproduction; kept out to avoid shipping unused data).
inputs/*.json

# Transient, regenerated by `make analyze` / `make render` / `reproduce.sh`
claims.json
PILOT_RESULTS.md
results/

# Environment / OS / build cruft
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/.fuse_hidden*
*.aux
*.log
*.out

# Not part of this artifact (mislabeled upload = Paper 1's manuscript in plain format)
IEEE-Access-Submission-Checklist.pdf

# ── Intentionally COMMITTED (results + provenance) ──
#   config/slots.yaml                                    results-gate contract
#   data/frozen/*.freeze.json                            capture hash receipts
#   claims_<pair>.json, results_<pair>.md, tempsweep_*   released per-pair results
